WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.462
Operating DNSSEC is mostly key
management, automated and audited.

2
00:00:04.462 --> 00:00:08.711
NIST recommends a hardware security
module for the important keys,

3
00:00:08.711 --> 00:00:11.593
signatures valid for
about five to seven days,

4
00:00:11.593 --> 00:00:15.613
and it prefers ECDSA, because
smaller keys keep responses small.

5
00:00:15.613 --> 00:00:17.688
The slide has the full parameters.

6
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:22.300
Moving a signed zone has its own
careful sequence, run in Phase 3.

7
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.700
Don't start a key
rollover during the move.

8
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.383
Keep the old signing until the new chain
validates from an independent checker,

9
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:31.725
and only then stop signing at the source.

10
00:00:31.725 --> 00:00:35.988
Watch the validators, because
clients only see generic failures.

11
00:00:35.988 --> 00:00:39.978
An AD-signed internal zone
moving to Azure Private DNS,

12
00:00:39.978 --> 00:00:43.349
which can't sign, is a
documented risk decision.

13
00:00:43.349 --> 00:00:47.690
And retire old trust anchors after
the ninety-day validation period.
